     1	"""PLAN-190 W1 — Workflow launch ledger: persist BEFORE dispatch, guard resumes.
     2	
     3	Why this exists
     4	---------------
     5	The harness persists a Workflow run's ``args`` only when the run ENDS
     6	(``<session>/workflows/wf_<id>.json``, status completed/killed/failed), never
     7	its script hash, the code revision it ran against, nor anything at launch
     8	time. A run interrupted by a process death leaves no record of the exact call;
     9	an operator who re-issues the call from memory changes the runner's result
    10	cache key (prompt + opts) and re-executes finished phases. Measured on one
    11	consumer (S354): 15.5 % of phase starts never produced a result and 16 % of
    12	starts were re-executions; two incidents (17 slices re-implemented after a
    13	prompt edit in flight; 11 slices regressed after args rebuilt from memory)
    14	are exactly the class this module closes.
    15	
    16	What it records (one manifest per Workflow tool call)
    17	-----------------------------------------------------
    18	``launch_id``, instant, ``session_id``, ``tool_use_id``, ``cwd``; the script
    19	fingerprint (``sha256`` + size) AND a snapshot of the effective script bytes
    20	(``<launch_id>.script``) so the exact call is reproducible even when the
    21	harness never wrote its own copy (a run killed by a process death) or the
    22	file changed afterwards; the ``args`` as a LITERAL canonical JSON (an absent
    23	``args`` field is recorded as ABSENT, distinct from ``null``; never
    24	truncated — the hash is over the full content); ``resumeFromRunId``;
    25	``name``/``description``; the code revision of ``cwd`` — ENRICHED AFTER the
    26	manifest is on disk, with a git budget far below the hook's 5-second timeout
    27	(``--no-optional-locks``, unknown on failure); the ``run_id`` once the
    28	PostToolUse half binds it, with the ``bind_method`` recorded.
    29	
    30	Files live under the project's runtime state dir
    31	(``_lib.runtime_paths.runtime_state_dir()/launches``): one JSON per launch
    32	(atomic write, mode 0600), one ``.script`` snapshot, and an append-only
    33	``launches.jsonl`` index (``launch`` / ``bind`` / ``unbind`` / ``orphan``
    34	lines).
    35	
    36	The guard (debate r1 + pair-rail r1 shaped it)
    37	----------------------------------------------
    38	A call with ``resumeFromRunId`` is compared against the manifest BOUND to
    39	that run.
    40	* ``args`` differ (per top-level key) ⇒ **block** (the demonstrated loss).
    41	* script ``sha256`` differs ⇒ **advisory** by default (recorded as
    42	  ``mismatch_script_advisory``; the substrate re-executes only the phases
    43	  whose prompt changed, and resuming over a fixed script is a legitimate
    44	  route); ``CEO_WORKFLOW_SCRIPT_GUARD=enforce`` turns it into a block.
    45	* args identical but either script hash unavailable ⇒ **inconclusive**
    46	  (allowed, recorded) — an unverifiable script comparison is never turned into
    47	  a block nor into a match; different args still block on their own.
    48	* no bound manifest ⇒ ``no_manifest`` (allowed, recorded).
    49	* a manifest bound heuristically (``by_single_unbound``) never sustains a
    50	  block, args or script alike (``weak_bind`` recorded; advisory instead).
    51	* ONE override path for every block, and it lives in the CALL, never on
    52	  disk: ``CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_FORCE=1`` in the process environment, or the
    53	  call itself declaring it — ``description`` starting with the exact prefix
    54	  ``CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_FORCE:`` followed by a non-empty reason. The
    55	  declaration is visible in the transcript, applies to that one call and
    56	  nothing else, and leaves no state behind to read back (so no race and no
    57	  parse of stored override state). Result ``mismatch_forced``, announced;
    58	  the reason is recorded in the manifest, never echoed.
    59	* the recorded manifest is VALIDATED before it is compared
    60	  (``manifest_problem``: schema, args canonical/hash/presence consistency,
    61	  script hash against its snapshot bytes, run id and bind method shapes);
    62	  an inconsistent record is ``inconclusive`` — never evidence of a match
    63	  nor of a mismatch. Any exception inside the guard is also recorded as
    64	  ``inconclusive`` with the manifest still written.
    65	* ``CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_GUARD=0`` puts the whole guard in advisory mode while
    66	  keeping the ledger; ``CEO_WORKFLOW_LEDGER=0`` disables the hook.
    67	* a launch the guard blocked stays in the index (``blocked: true``) and is
    68	  never a candidate for heuristic binding.
    69	
    70	The block reason is COUNTS-ONLY: it never carries operator text (arg key
    71	names, values, or an unvalidated run id) — the reason reaches the model and
    72	an instruction-adjacent channel is closed by removal, not by escaping
    73	(PLAN-179 r22). The detail (which keys) lives in the manifest.
    74	
    75	Binding (PostToolUse)
    76	---------------------
    77	By ``tool_use_id`` when the event carries one: found ⇒ bind (``by_tool_use``);
    78	not found ⇒ an ``orphan`` index line, NO bind. Without ``tool_use_id``: bind
    79	only when EXACTLY ONE unbound launch exists in the same session
    80	(``by_single_unbound``); otherwise ``orphan``. Never across sessions. The
    81	operator's ``ceo-launches.py bind`` closes an orphan by hand.
