templates/settings/settings.stack.otel.json:6:  "_no_egress_comment": "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT points at http://127.0.0.1:4318 — the LOCAL loopback sink ONLY. The sink (.claude/scripts/otel-local-sink.py) binds 127.0.0.1, opens NO outbound socket, and writes JSONL to the project state dir. There is NO cloud OTel backend in this fragment by design: the meta-repo's telemetry (which can contain Owner source snippets) never leaves the workstation. An adopter who WANTS cloud export uses the ADR-035 exporter (otel-export.py) with its 6-mitigation defense bundle + CEO_OTEL_ALLOWED_HOSTS allowlist — a deliberate, separately-gated choice. Do NOT repoint OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT at a non-loopback host in this fragment; that would turn a no-egress dashboard into an exfil channel without the ADR-035 redaction pipeline.",
