templates/settings/settings.base.json:644:  "_night_mode_deny_surface_comment": "PLAN-165 P1-corrected (D2 + round-2 findings NM-01/NM-03 + codex CX-1) — under defaultMode=acceptEdits a tool Edit/Write is auto-accepted, so every file that can DECIDE the next session's posture is deny-listed: (1) .claude/settings.local.json, the per-machine overlay (gitignored) that decides the NEXT session's permission posture; (2) .claude/state/night-mode.json, the night-mode marker/snapshot whose prev_value is restored into the overlay by night-mode off — a posture write BY PROXY (NM-01); (3) .claude/scripts/night-mode.py, the single sanctioned writer itself (NM-03). HONEST SCOPE (CX-1): per-TOOL deny entries close only the Edit/Write rail; the Bash rail is closed by _CANONICAL_GUARDS in check_canonical_edit.py (all three paths listed) + kernel-tier listing of the two state files. The script writes as a PROCESS, never via the Edit/Write tools, so the deny costs no legitimate path. The Write() twins were REMOVED in S292: the current harness (>=2.1.216) does NOT consult Write(path) rules in its file-permission check (the CLI emits an active warning for such rules) and the Edit(path) entries cover ALL file-editing tools — the same class PLAN-161 C1 removed from the credential-read baseline; the old-CLI residual documented there is now accepted for the posture files too, with the real defense on the _CANONICAL_GUARDS/kernel rails (CX-1). Mirrors .claude/settings.json in the framework repo (dogfood parity) — the three entries are byte-identical in both files.",
